<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Adolphus Frederick VI, Grand Duke of Mecklenburg-Strelitz</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1882–1918</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Adolf Frederick VI of Mecklenburg-Strelitz</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Adolphus Frederick VI was the last reigning Grand Duke of Mecklenburg-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/strelitz">Strelitz</a>, from 1914 to 1918. Unmarried, he took his own life in February 1918, leaving no direct heir and the succession disputed between distant relatives. The grand duchy was left without a ruler when the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-revolution-of-1918-1919">November Revolution</a> of 1918 turned it into the Free State of Mecklenburg-Strelitz.</p></div>
